  "result": "I added `click.KeyValue`, which parses `key=value` into a `(key, value)` tuple. The full test suite passes (1913 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed), including 7 new KeyValue tests.\n\nUsage matches your example:\n\n```python\n@click.option('--set', type=click.KeyValue())\n```\n\n- **Splitting:** it splits on the first `=`, so `a=b=c` gives `('a', 'b=c')`.\n- **Empty value:** `a=` is accepted and gives `('a', '')`.\n- **Errors:** input with no `=`, an empty key (`=1`), or an empty string fails with `... is not a valid key=value pair.` and exits with code 2.\n- **Whitespace:** I don't strip spaces, so `' a = 1'` gives `(' a ', ' 1')`. Say if you want stripping.\n\nChanges:\n- `src/click/types.py`: the new `KeyValue` class, placed after `UUIDParameterType`.\n- `src/click/__init__.py`: exports `KeyValue`.\n- `tests/test_basic.py`: option tests for valid and invalid input, plus a direct `convert` test.\n- `docs/api.md` and `docs/parameter-types.md`: documentation entries.\n- `CHANGES.md`: a new \"Version 8.6.0 / Unreleased\" entry. The project is at 8.5.0, so the `versionadded` note and the version heading are my guess at the next version.\n\nRuff and mypy aren't installed in the venv, so I didn't run them. I checked line length by hand and found no new long lines. Nothing is committed.",
